{title: Angels from the Realms of Glory}
{artist: James Montgomery & Henry Smart}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[Bb]Angels from the [F]realms of [Bb]glory, [Eb]wing your [Bb]flight o'er [F]all the earth;
[Bb]ye who sang cre[F]ation's [Bb]story [Eb]now pro[Bb]claim Mes[F]siah's [Bb]birth:

Chorus
[Bb]Come and worship, [F]come and worship —
[Eb]worship [Bb]Christ, the [F]newborn [Bb]King.

Verse 2
[Bb]Shepherds, in the field [F]abiding, Watching o'er [Bb]your flocks [Eb]by night, God [Bb]with us is [F]now residing; Yonder shines
[Bb]the infant light: Come and worship, [Bb]come and [Eb]worship, Worship Christ, the [Bb]newborn King.

Verse 3
[Bb]Sages, leave your contemplations, [F]Brighter visions beam [Bb]afar; [Eb]Seek the great [Bb]Desire of nations; [F]Ye have seen His
[Bb]natal star. Come and worship, come [Bb]and [Eb]worship, Worship Christ, the newborn [Bb]King.

Verse 4
[Bb]Saints, before the altar [F]bending, Watching long [Bb]in [Eb]hope and fear; [Bb]Suddenly the Lord, [F]descending, In His temple
[Bb]shall appear. Come and worship, come [Bb]and [Eb]worship, Worship Christ, the newborn [Bb]King.

Verse 5
[Bb]Sinners, wrung with true [F]repentance, Doomed for [Bb]guilt to [Eb]endless pains, Justice [Bb]now revokes the [F]sentence, Mercy calls you;
[Bb]break your chains. Come and worship, [Bb]come and [Eb]worship, Worship Christ, the [Bb]newborn King.
